(window.COURSE_SOURCES = window.COURSE_SOURCES || {})["vintage-reselling"] = "Sources were read through search and fetch excerpts on 11/10/2026. No source was read in full, so treat every rule as a pointer to check on the current page.\n\n**Read in part (excerpts):**\n- GOV.UK: Selling goods or services on a digital platform; Tax-free allowances on property and trading income; Distance selling; Deal in items made of or containing ivory; Ivory pre-1918 exemption certificate.\n- HMRC Business Income Manual: BIM86000 (opening); BIM20205 (opening only; the badges of trade list came from a secondary accountants' guide).\n- Business Companion (Trading Standards): Am I in business?; Second-hand upholstered furniture; Second-hand electrical goods; Hallmarking.\n- legislation.gov.uk: Consumer Rights Act 2015 sections 2 and 9 (section 9 opening only) and the Explanatory Notes; Furniture and Furnishings (Fire) (Safety) Regulations 1988.\n- eBay.co.uk fee pages for private and business sellers (updated 30/09/2026); Vinted UK fee page.\n\n**Secondary sources (not primary):** IAK Accountants on the trading allowance (11/09/2026); underpriced.app on Etsy vintage rules (28/02/2026).\n\n**Not read or not confirmed:**\n- Etsy UK fee rates (the fetched page was partly in Spanish) and Etsy's own vintage policy.\n- Depop, Facebook Marketplace and other platforms.\n- Irish Revenue and Irish consumer law (the Revenue pages returned errors). Northern Ireland guidance is published by NI Business Info and was not read.\n- Full text of Consumer Rights Act section 9 and sections on risk in transit, the Digital Markets, Competition and Consumers Act 2024, the Trade Marks Act 1994, jewellery metal-content rules, toy and baby-goods safety rules, VAT, Making Tax Digital.\n\n**Our own material (not sourced):** sourcing channel comparison, dating clues, condition scale, cleaning advice, photography and listing advice, packing and shipping practice, and the decimalisation date of 15/02/1971. All invented numbers in worked examples are labelled illustrative.\n\n**Fees change.** Percentages in worked examples are those shown on eBay UK's business seller page for the Antiques category when read. Check your own category and invoice, including any VAT.\n";
